*> PLB-Q017 fetch-after-close: a FETCH or CLOSE of an SQL cursor after
*> its CLOSE, with no OPEN between.
IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. FETCHCLS.
DATA DIVISION.
WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
01  WS-ID                   PIC S9(9) COMP.
    EXEC SQL DECLARE ACCT-CUR CURSOR FOR
        SELECT ACCT_ID FROM ACCOUNT
    END-EXEC.
PROCEDURE DIVISION.
MAIN-LINE.
    *> Reported: a FETCH after the CLOSE, and a second CLOSE.
    EXEC SQL OPEN ACCT-CUR END-EXEC
    EXEC SQL CLOSE ACCT-CUR END-EXEC
    EXEC SQL FETCH ACCT-CUR INTO :WS-ID END-EXEC
    EXEC SQL OPEN ACCT-CUR END-EXEC
    EXEC SQL CLOSE ACCT-CUR END-EXEC.
    DISPLAY WS-ID.
    EXEC SQL CLOSE ACCT-CUR END-EXEC.
    *> Not reported: opened again first, a PERFORM between.
    EXEC SQL OPEN ACCT-CUR END-EXEC
    EXEC SQL FETCH ACCT-CUR INTO :WS-ID END-EXEC
    EXEC SQL CLOSE ACCT-CUR END-EXEC
    PERFORM OPEN-ACCT
    EXEC SQL FETCH ACCT-CUR INTO :WS-ID END-EXEC
    STOP RUN.
OPEN-ACCT.
    EXEC SQL OPEN ACCT-CUR END-EXEC.
